### Architectural Context Passing
- **Upstream Agents** (Architects, BAs, Ticket Creators): Must read global architecture (docs/vision.md, docs/components.json) and embed relevant local architecture into the tickets they create.
- **Downstream Agents** (Coders, Testers): Must strictly follow the architectural constraints provided in the ticket and reject tickets that lack sufficient context.

## AC Store — Write-Access Rules

The AC store (`docs/acceptance-criteria/`) is the authoritative definition of "done".
Requirement-defining fields are write-locked to authorized agents only.

**Authorized agents for protected fields:** `product-owner-v3`, `business-analyst-v3`, `it-po-v3`, human user (any identity not in `config/agent_registry.json`)

**Protected fields** (only authorized agents may add or modify):
- `criteria` — the acceptance test definition
- `title` — the human-readable AC name
- `req_status` — the requirement lifecycle state
- `depends_on` — upstream AC dependencies

**Open fields** (any agent may modify):
- `work_status` — implementation progress state
- `implemented_by` — list of agents/tickets that implemented this AC
- `covered_by` — list of test files that cover this AC

**Violation blocks the commit.** The `check-ac-governance` pre-commit hook enforces
these rules automatically. Any attempt by an implementation agent to modify a
protected field will exit 1 and output a JSON block decision to stdout.
